# The fusions that owe no sum in one quantity because a layer the sum reads leaves it unstated.
# One row per (composed layer, quantity), shaped like the other suspension grounds so the union
# stays a union, with the unstated layers named in `note`.
#
# A missing term is not a zero
#   `Σ converted parts` joins each part's figure, so a part that files its draw as `unmeasured`
#   would simply drop out of the draw sum, and the sum would come out short by exactly the figure
#   nobody measured. A composed layer that files no draw has nothing to compare a sum with. Either
#   way the equality is not owed, for that quantity and no other, which is the same argument an
#   unsized elimination makes.
#
# A derived figure is not unstated
#   A layer filing the quantity as its fusion's sum files an output, which the receiver computes, so it is
#   not a gap and nothing here reads it as one. A part's is computed through its own fusion by
#   composition/derived_quantities.sqlc, and composition/underived_parts.sqlc lifts the sum where
#   that computation cannot finish. A composed layer's owes no equality, and
#   composition/derived_fusions.sqlc says so.
#
# Per quantity, never for the whole fusion
#   A fusion whose parts file no draw still owes its demand and nameplate sums exactly, so
#   `quantity` is always set here. A caller computing one quantity's sum reads
#   `quantity IS NULL OR quantity = <that one>`, and this arm answers only for its own.
-- layers/summed_quantities.sqlc without a figure on a part or on the composed layer, and not a derivation, per fusion.
SELECT u.composition, u.composed_layer, u.quantity,
       'the quantity is not stated on every layer the sum reads' AS suspended_because,
       string_agg(u.layer || ' ' || coalesce(u.absent::text, 'unstated'), ', ' ORDER BY u.layer)
           AS note
FROM (
    SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer, s.quantity,
           p.part_filing || '/' || p.part_layer AS layer, s.absent
    FROM      (
        :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
    ) p
    JOIN      (
        :compose(layers/summed_quantities.sqlc)
    ) s ON s.filing = p.part_filing AND s.layer = p.part_layer
    WHERE s.low IS NULL
      AND s.derivation IS NULL
    UNION ALL
    SELECT q.filing, q.layer, q.quantity, 'the composed layer', q.absent
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/fusion_quantities.sqlc)
    ) q
    WHERE q.low IS NULL
      AND q.derivation IS NULL
) u
GROUP BY u.composition, u.composed_layer, u.quantity
